inimum payment was {$110.00} and the old purchase now read {$100.00} .. On XX/XX/XXXX ( today ) I again called Synchrony to fix the issue.. I asked to speak with a manager or a claims escalation member.. The rep XXXX wanted to help before the transfer .. After some waiting she came back and said that they are unable to allocate the extra funds to the smaller payment .. She said a letter was sent out on XXXX.. I never received a letter and when I asked her how come the representative from the XX/XX/XXXX phone call never mentioned the letter and said she fixed the situation she had no response.. I then asked for a supervisor and was transferred to XXXX .. XXXX reiterated several times that I have two accounts .. One with a minimum of {$67.00} and the other with a minimum of {$48.00}.. He said that they are unable to allocate the extra funds to the older/smaller payment.. When I asked why if I have two accounts and two minimum payments am I not allowed to make two separate payments and pay off one he didn't have an explanation.. I have tried three times to rectify the situation to no avail and in fact I was blatantly lied to.. Although we always pay way more than the minimum due it's false advertising.. I signed up for minimum payment and they have changed the terms of agreement .. At this point XXXX XXXX me there's nothing he can do and no matter how much extra money I pay a month they will only allocate the {$48.00} min due to the older account.. The old account will now not fall off until XX/XX/XXXX.. This is unacceptable and I told XXXX I would be filing a complaint with you as well as my local congressman who will notify the AG.. It's absolutely insane that something so minor has to escalate to this level",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,SYNCHRONY FINANCIAL,FL,32164,,Web,2026-05-19,Closed with explanation,Yes
