fice and spoke with another representative. I was then informed that the repayment plan had been canceled and that our account may be proceeding toward foreclosure. This is completely unacceptable given our consistent efforts to comply and communicate. I talked with a supervisorXXXXXXXX XXXX  who also had no answers and didn't know any way to help us.\n\nAdditionally, we are aware of multiple lawsuits and class action complaints that Shellpoint has faced related to loss mitigation failures. Given our current experience, this raises serious concerns about how our case has been handled.\n\nI have documentation of all emails, phone calls, and voicemails made over the past several months. It is deeply concerning that after three months of persistent outreach, we have been ignored entirely. This level of service is not appropriate for a company responsible for managing family homes.\n\nAt this point, I am requesting:\n\nImmediate escalation of this matter to a supervisor or executive-level representative\nA clear explanation of why the repayment plan was canceled without notice\nImmediate guidance on reinstating the repayment plan\nDirect communication from someone who has the authority to resolve this issue\nWe have lived in our home for 11 years and have never experienced anything like this prior to working with Shellpoint. I am simply asking for assistance in resolving this matter and reinstating our repayment plan, which we have made every effort to uphold.\n\nPlease treat this matter as urgent. I expect a prompt response and direct contact from someone in a position to assist.\n\nThank you for your time, and I look forward to hearing from you as soon as possible.\n\nThank you,\n\nXXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX. We also were told to apply in the online portal which we did multiple times.""",Company believes it acted appropriately as authorized by contract or law,"Shellpoint Partners, LLC",GA,30252,,Web,2026-05-20,Closed with exp